# Additions to table inet greenhouse_egress for the body double app
# (deploy/body-double.md). install-body-double.sh merges the set into the table
# and the rules into chain output, and adds the same to the running ruleset
# with `nft add` (a reload would empty the running services' cgroup sets).
# systemd fills the set through the unit's NFTSet=.
#
# The app may reach the kernel on loopback and nothing else: no name lookups,
# no public web, never the LAN or the tailnet. It originates calls only to the
# kernel (registration, /api/notify, /api/notify/retire). The kernel's calls to
# the app on 127.0.0.1:4107 are inbound, and their replies are established.
#
#     set body_double_cgroups {
#         type cgroupsv2
#         comment "systemd-managed greenhouse-body-double.service cgroups"
#     }
#
socket cgroupv2 level 2 @body_double_cgroups ct state established,related accept
socket cgroupv2 level 2 @body_double_cgroups ip daddr 127.0.0.1 tcp dport 4000 accept
socket cgroupv2 level 2 @body_double_cgroups counter drop
